+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | In Progress          |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates caller-supplied `input` against the resolved tool definition's `inputSchema` before invoking the executor. On failure it returns a `ToolResponse` describing the constraint violation so the model can recover within `DEFAULT_MAX_TOOL_ROUNDS` instead of failing the conversation with a transport error, while reserving throws for unknown tool names.
+
+## Validation contract
+
+- When `input` violates a `required` field or `enum` constraint, `execute` returns a `ToolResponse` naming the failing property path and constraint and does not invoke the executor ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field or enum constraint without calling the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L11)).
+- A wrong-typed field is rejected without type coercion, naming the property path and expected type while never exposing any payload value in the returned text or log lines ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field naming path and expected type without coercing or leaking values](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L47)).
+- Registering a static tool compiles its `inputSchema` at registration time and throws an error naming the tool if the schema cannot be compiled ([validated by: throws at register time for a schema that cannot be compiled and names the tool](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L103)).
+- A function-valued `ToolDefinitionSource` validates against the schema current on each `execute` call, and valid inputs with unlisted extra properties pass through to the executor unmodified without injecting defaults or `additionalProperties: false` ([validated by: validates dynamic tool definitions against the current schema and forwards extra properties unmodified](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L121)).
+- In the orchestrator tool loop, a schema rejection reaches the model as a `tool_result` so `processMessage` resolves when the model supplies a corrected retry ([validated by: returns a validation rejection to the provider so processMessage resolves on a corrected retry](../../src/orchestration/chatOrchestrator.acceptance.test.ts#L8)).
+- A static tool definition compiles its `inputSchema` once at `register` time rather than recompiling on subsequent `execute` calls.
+- Calling `execute` with an unregistered tool name throws `Unknown tool: <name>`.
